<title>SWITZERLAND: Ciba, Sandoz shares lower.</title>
<headline>Ciba, Sandoz shares lower.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Ciba-Geigy AG and Sandoz AG were lower in late Swiss trading after news that the U.S. Federal Trade Commission had conditionally approved their merger into Novartis AG.</p>
<p>The shares had jumped briefly when the companies called a news conference to announce the news, then retreated to Monday's closing levels.</p>
<p>At 1524 GMT, just before the close, Sandoz bearers were down 10 Swiss francs to 1,519 and Ciba registered stock was off four francs to 1,623.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
